# "Goblin" is a creature type word in Howlsquad Heavy's text (CR 612.2), so Artificial Evolution changing it to Cat changes what its
# max speed mana ability counts: "{T}: Add {R} for each Cat you control". Howlsquad Heavy and a Savannah Lions come down in turn 1's
# first main phase (speed 1). Each of Bot1's combats makes a hasty Goblin token that must attack: on turn 1 it alone hits an empty board
# (speed 2), on turns 3 and 5 the Lions and every token do (speed 3, 4). In turn 5's second main phase Bot1 controls four Goblins (the
# Heavy and three tokens) and one Cat. The change rewrites the Heavy's type line too (CR 612.1), so it is now a Cat Mercenary itself:
# two Cats, and the Heavy taps for exactly {R}{R}, not one {R} per Goblin token.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Howlsquad Heavy
Savannah Lions
Artificial Evolution
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

